#!/usr/bin/env bash
# ============================================================================
# mycelium — shim dispatcher
# ============================================================================
# The Go binary `mycelium` takes precedence if installed globally (on PATH).
# If not found, this shim provides a friendly error message directing users
# to the install script, and points them to ./mycelium-dev for the legacy
# bash write-path (bootstrapping, heartbeat control, etc.).
# ============================================================================

# Check if mycelium is available on PATH (the Go binary)
if command -v mycelium &>/dev/null; then
  # Go binary is installed and available on PATH
  # Delegate to it with all arguments
  exec mycelium "$@"
fi

# Go binary not found — user needs to install it
cat >&2 <<'EOF'
The `mycelium` command is now the Go binary (faster, cross-platform).

To install:
  curl -sSL https://github.com/Qubit-Capital/maverick/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash

Then restart your shell and try again.

For the legacy write-path (bootstrap, start, stop, dump, restore, fork, sync, drift, ingest-repo, inject):
  ./mycelium-dev <command> [args]

EOF
exit 1
